# 07 §4.6, the home section: what the reach asks of the class
edit(CH7, """the class of `Inconstant`, which holds the member's effects, fails it at the member (`Inconstant.not_constant_at`).
- **How what lies outside is divided.**""", """the class of `Inconstant`, which holds the member's effects, fails it at the member (`Inconstant.not_constant_at`).
- **What the reach asks of the class.** With no regularity assumed, everything downstream of a member lies on its line under a class exactly where everything downstream of it is alike to it (`«后皆同类则后皆续»`, `«后皆续当且仅当后皆同类»`), that is, where the class holds the effects of the member and of each stage of its line (`«后皆续当且仅当自与线皆闭»`). So the reach asks that the class hold the member's effects (`«后皆续则所缘同于»`), and, like the condition at the member's class (`«亡而网续则本类不至终有常»`), it excludes a line from the member that ends while its last stage still conditions something (`«亡而网续则后不皆续»`; the organism's case in `FiniteFamilies.member_no_reach`). With the member's effects held, where the member conditions something, the condition at its class gives the reach (`«本类常闭则后皆续»`), and more: the class then holds the effects of every alike occurrence, on the member's line or not (`«本类常闭则所缘同类»`). The laws above cannot drop the condition (`Inconstant.not_constant_at`, `Inconstant.not_all_follow`), but the reach does not need it. In a net where a member conditions one thing, that thing conditions another, an occurrence alike to the member conditions a further thing, and nothing else is conditioned, the class that holds all of them but that further thing holds the member's effects and everything downstream of the member lies on its line, while the class fails the condition at the member and does not hold the effects of the other occurrence, which lies off the member's line (`OtherLeaves.reach_without_condition`, `OtherLeaves.other_not_held`, `OtherLeaves.other_off_line`).
- **How what lies outside is divided.**""")

# the home section: the condition where the member acts, and the division through its own leaving effects
edit(CH7, """give the same verdict (`«外分唯系出类之同»`). Where the class holds the effects of a member that conditions something, the condition keeps every alike occurrence's effects in the class (`«本类常闭则所缘同类»`), so every division that gives the member the same class gives the same verdict (`«闭则外分无关»`, applied both ways).""",
     """give the same verdict (`«外分唯系出类之同»`). Where the member conditions something, the condition at its class is that the member and each alike occurrence follow each other: whatever an alike occurrence conditions is alike to something the member conditions, and whatever the member conditions, each alike occurrence that conditions anything conditions something alike to it (`«本类常当且仅当与己相随»`). So how what lies outside is divided bears on it only through what is alike to the member's own effects that leave the class: two classes that give the member the same class, and agree on what is alike to each of those effects, give the same verdict (`«外分唯系己出之同»`). Where the class holds the member's effects, none of them leaves, so every division that gives the member the same class gives the same verdict (`«闭则外分无关»`, applied both ways).""")

# P2: what the condition is where one acts
edit(CH7, """How the class divides what lies outside oneself enters through what is alike to an effect that an occurrence alike to oneself leaves out; which division P2 reads is argued below.""",
     """Where one acts, the condition is that oneself and each occurrence alike to oneself follow each other in what they condition (`«本类常当且仅当与己相随»`), so how the class divides what lies outside oneself enters only through what is alike to one's own effects that leave it (`«外分唯系己出之同»`); which division P2 reads is argued below.""")

# the conclusion: what the reach is, and what P2 and P4 do for it
edit(CH7, """Given the regularity of P2, P4 is equivalent to everything downstream of one's acts being alike to oneself (`«本类常则闭当且仅当后皆同类»`), and, given P4 as well, everything downstream of one's acts lies on one's line (`«本类常闭则后皆续»`). So the reach rests on one premise, holding one's effects, carried on by the regularity. The regularity does real work: where it fails at one's own class, holding one's effects need give nothing beyond the first step (`Inconstant.not_constant_at`, `Inconstant.not_all_follow`). P4 cannot be dropped at all: an effect not alike to oneself lies on no line under one's class (`«线内同类»`), as `Unclosed` shows for a line that runs through a condition.""",
     """The reach is exactly that everything downstream of one's acts is alike to oneself, with no regularity assumed (`«后皆续当且仅当后皆同类»`): that the class of one's line hold the effects of oneself and of each stage of one's line (`«后皆续当且仅当自与线皆闭»`). P4 is its first step and cannot be dropped at all (`«后皆续则所缘同于»`): an effect not alike to oneself lies on no line from oneself under one's class (`«线内同类»`), as `Unclosed` shows for a line that runs through a condition. P2 carries P4 on: given P2, P4 is equivalent to everything downstream of one's acts being alike to oneself (`«本类常则闭当且仅当后皆同类»`), and, given P4 as well, everything downstream of one's acts lies on one's line (`«本类常闭则后皆续»`). The regularity does real work: where it fails at one's own class, holding one's effects need give nothing beyond the first step (`Inconstant.not_constant_at`, `Inconstant.not_all_follow`). But it is not the only way: without it, a class can hold one's effects and have everything downstream of one's acts on one's line (`OtherLeaves.reach_without_condition`), and, given P4 and acting, the regularity gives more than the reach asks, the holding of the effects of every occurrence alike to oneself, on one's line or not (`«本类常闭则所缘同类»`, `OtherLeaves.other_not_held`). So what the path needs of P2 and P4 is one thing, that the class of one's line hold the effects of oneself and of each stage of one's line; P4 is its first step, and P2 one regularity that carries that step on.""")

# the denial of P2: what is left without it, and what the denial it names takes away
edit(CH7, """Denying P2 is coherent, since one can presuppose the significance of a line that ends while its last stage still conditions something.
""", """Denying P2 is coherent, since one can presuppose the significance of a line that ends while its last stage still conditions something. Denying it does not by itself take the reach away: without P2, the reach holds exactly where the class of one's line holds the effects of oneself and of each stage of one's line (`«后皆续当且仅当自与线皆闭»`), as in `OtherLeaves`, where P2 fails through an occurrence alike to oneself off one's line. The denial just named takes it away: where one's line ends while its last stage still conditions something, not everything downstream of one's acts lies on one's line (`«亡而网续则后不皆续»`).
""")

# which class P2 reads: the division through one's own leaving effects
edit(CH7, """So read, P2 is idle to how what one leaves out is divided wherever one acts and holds one's effects (`«闭则外分无关»`), and so for the path's conclusion, which needs P4. Where one does not hold them, the division enters P2 only through what is alike to an effect that an occurrence alike to oneself leaves out (`«外分唯系出类之同»`). What a finer division adds is a demand on what one's acts leave outside: every occurrence alike to oneself that conditions anything must leave something of each kind that any of them leaves (`FinerOutside`), the kinds being fixed by how what lies outside oneself is divided, not by oneself.""",
     """So read, wherever one acts the division enters P2 only through what is alike to one's own effects that leave one's class (`«外分唯系己出之同»`), so P2 is idle to it wherever one also holds one's effects (`«闭则外分无关»`), and so for the path's conclusion, which needs P4. What a finer division adds, where one acts, is a demand on what one's acts leave outside: every occurrence alike to oneself that conditions anything must leave something of each kind that one leaves, and nothing of a kind one does not leave (`«本类常当且仅当与己相随»`, `FinerOutside`), the kinds being fixed by how what lies outside oneself is divided, not by oneself.""")

# P-20: P2 where one acts
edit(DOSSIER, """- (P2) The self whose continuation is presupposed is a line under a class on the root, and that class is constant up to the net's end at oneself: whatever an occurrence alike to oneself conditions, every occurrence alike to oneself that conditions anything conditions something alike to it. Quote""",
     """- (P2) The self whose continuation is presupposed is a line under a class on the root, and that class is constant up to the net's end at oneself: whatever an occurrence alike to oneself conditions, every occurrence alike to oneself that conditions anything conditions something alike to it. Where one acts, the condition is that oneself and each occurrence alike to oneself follow each other in what they condition: whatever an occurrence alike to oneself conditions is alike to something one conditions, and whatever one conditions, each alike occurrence that conditions anything conditions something alike to it (`«本类常当且仅当与己相随»`, a root theorem). Quote""")

